window.docContents[168].resolve({"/#sum-products-units":{"contents":"Generally speaking, types that offer multiple constructors are called sum types, while types whose single constructor takes multiple arguments are called product types.\nThese terms are related to sums and products used in ordinary arithmetic.\nThe relationship is easiest to see when the types involved contain a finite number of values.\nIf  and  are types that contain n and k distinct values, respectively, then  contains n + k distinct values and  contains n \\times k distinct values.\nFor instance,  has two values:  and , and  has one value: .\nThe product  has the two values  and , and the sum  has the three values , , and .\nSimilarly, 2 \\times 1 = 2, and 2 + 1 = 3.\n\n","context":"Functional Programming in Lean\u0009Getting to Know Lean\u0009Polymorphism\u0009More Built-In Datatypes","header":"1.6.3.6. Naming: Sums, Products, and Units","id":"/#sum-products-units"}});